From 3b0bee0a009c630d6fee36f4c3979c78c41b8a87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 18:13:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08032/11362] Reverting G3 buys nothing: it moves ka59's
 failure from the gate to the planner at ~8x the wall clock

Operator-directed evaluation of reverting change G3 of 0cb1f23f3 (the goal
gate's budget unit: unique grids -> engine calls, closing an 11x
permissiveness gap against plan_in_model). Measured on ka59, engine
341f776c9, offline arcade, both arms from the canonical repo path:

  G3-reverted gate  -> satisfiable at 12,435 unique grids, depth 11  (190.9s)
  plan_in_model     -> NO PLAN, max_nodes_reached, 20,006 nodes       (21.2s)
  HEAD gate         -> honest refusal, budget_exhausted               (26.8s)

So the revert spends ~212s to reach the same no-plan HEAD reaches in 26.8s.
A ka59 plan does exist -- canonical length 11, replays to reached_level 1 --
but needs 137,347 nodes, which no gate change reaches. G3's justification
("a gate must not out-search the planner it guards") is now measured rather
than argued: arms B then D ARE the false-certification-then-planner-failure
it was introduced to prevent. VERDICT: do not revert.

The prescribed remedy (split budget_exhausted from degenerate_goal_predicate)
was already shipped complete in 1b2e66f36. What was actually broken:

- The gate had NO max_nodes knob at all. All three call sites pass none and
  nothing read an env var, so the commit's own "max_nodes is compute and may
  be raised" was unreachable for the gate -- while the planner has had
  CARNOT_ARC_PLAN_MAX_NODES since REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-15. Adds
  CARNOT_ARC_GOAL_GATE_MAX_NODES: dev-only, unset in production, default
  bit-identical, malformed values fall back, explicit args still win. Compute
  only; no predicate touched. This also retracts a false row in this
  session's own earlier knob table, which claimed the reinduce path's planner
  was not overridable -- it is, via _guided_plan_in_model.

- A false MECHANISM was justifying a correct design, in production and in its
  test: the inner break cannot leave q empty (it fires immediately after
  q.append, measurably leaving frontier_remaining == 1). The real drain is
  the dedup path. Corrected additively in both places per never-prune; the
  wrong reason invites exactly the "simplification" mutation M3 encodes.

- arc_llm_reinduction.py had been citing ops/known-issues.md
  "budget-exhausted goal pre-veto" since 1b2e66f36; that entry did not exist.
  Written, rather than repointing away from it.

- Newly disclosed, not fixed: unit alignment does not align SEARCH ORDER. The
  gate is BFS; plan_in_model is best-first given a goal energy. Inert at
  defaults (flat binary energy ties FIFO -- why both measured 137,347), live
  under CARNOT_ARC_GRADED_GOAL_BIAS=1, which measured 2.3x worse anyway.

- The recorded "mutation-proven 7/7" claim for the dedup key stated no
  method, which this repo's default -n 4 makes unfalsifiable (a
  parent-process patch is discarded by xdist workers). Re-run under -n0: 7 of
  8, one REAL survivor -- dropping the dtype.kind guard crashes in a.min() on
  a string grid where HEAD short-circuits and keys correctly. Closed by a new
  test; now 8/8. The trap is recorded in known-issues.md so the next proof
  cannot be silently vacuous.

Also retracts a review claim that the mutation guard exits 0 while refusing:
an unarmed --check exits 1. The actionable half was applied -- a --snapshot
baseline was taken before the first test run, so the guard MEASURED (flagging
exactly the files hand-edited after it, all verified mine by diff) rather
than refusing.

Banked ARC levels remain 3/3 and the submission gate is NOT met. Nothing here
solved a level, played a game scored or offline, or measured a score.
Concurrent lane's three news-watch files deliberately left unstaged.
